The overall direction (centralizing DM_MAILBOX/MPFS_MBOX/MISC/
MPFS_SYSCONTROLLER implies into arch/riscv/cpu/mpfs/Kconfig instead of
duplicating them per-board) is a sensible cleanup, and 1/3 + 2/3 removing
the per-board implies while 3/3 adds them centrally does keep the net
Kconfig behavior equivalent for mpfs_generic and beaglev_fire once the full
series is applied.

One question on bisectability: since 1/3 and 2/3 remove these implies from
the two board Kconfigs before 3/3 adds the equivalent implies to the common
MPFS Kconfig, is there any other MPFS-based board besides mpfs_generic and
beaglev_fire that currently relies on getting DM_MAILBOX/MPFS_MBOX/MISC/
MPFS_SYSCONTROLLER transitively from one of these two boards' Kconfig
(e.g. via a "select BOARD_MICROCHIP_MPFS_GENERIC" chain, if such a thing
exists)? If not, bisection within the 3-patch series is fine since each
commit is self-contained for its own board; just confirming no third board
depends on mpfs_generic's or beaglev_fire's Kconfig as a side-channel for
these options.

Is there a 4th board (or MPFS variant) that should also have had its
per-board implies removed, to avoid duplicate "imply" statements from both
the common CPU Kconfig and that board's Kconfig now implying the same
symbols twice (harmless but redundant)?
